Object {
  "html": "<!doctype html><html lang=\\"en\\"><body style=\\"margin:0;padding:24px;background:#ffffff\\"><div style=\\"max-width:560px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:#0f172a\\"><p style=\\"margin:0 0 16px\\"><strong>25/100. High exposure.</strong><br>0 of 12 checks already pass. Here are the other 12, in the order to tackle them.</p><p style=\\"margin:0 0 8px\\"><strong>Critical</strong></p><ol style=\\"margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px\\"><li value=\\"1\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Move secret keys out of the app</strong><br>Anything in your JS bundle, app.config or EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables can be read from the app binary. Move each secret behind your own API, then rotate it: the old key is already exposed.<br><code style=\\"font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:14px\\">npx rnsec scan</code></li><li value=\\"2\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Verify: Block plain HTTP traffic</strong><br>Remove usesCleartextTraffic from AndroidManifest.xml and NSAllowsArbitraryLoads from Info.plist. If a dev server needs plain HTTP, allow only that domain, in a debug-only config.<br><code style=\\"font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:14px\\">git grep -nE &quot;usesCleartextTraffic|NSAllowsArbitraryLoads&quot;</code></li><li value=\\"3\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Enforce authorization on the backend</strong><br>Anyone can call your API without the app. Turn on Row Level Security on every Supabase table, or write Firebase Security Rules, then make each endpoint check who is asking and what they own.</li></ol><p style=\\"margin:0 0 8px\\"><strong>High</strong></p><ol style=\\"margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px\\"><li value=\\"4\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Verify: Store auth tokens in secure storage</strong><br>AsyncStorage and MMKV write plain files that a backup or a rooted device can read. Store access and refresh tokens with expo-secure-store (or react-native-keychain). This command lists the places that write a token today.<br><code style=\\"font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:14px\\">git grep -nE &quot;(AsyncStorage|MMKV|storage)\\\\.set.*[Tt]oken&quot;</code></li><li value=\\"5\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Clean secrets out of production logs</strong><br>Strip console.log from production builds with babel-plugin-transform-remove-console, and drop tokens, passwords and personal data in Sentry’s beforeSend.</li><li value=\\"6\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Validate deep link parameters</strong><br>Treat every deep link as untrusted input. Validate each parameter against what the screen expects, and ask for confirmation before a payment, a deletion or an account change.</li><li value=\\"7\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Verify: Lock down your WebViews</strong><br>Set originWhitelist to your own domains, and check event.nativeEvent.url in onMessage before acting on a message. Turn off javaScriptEnabled on WebViews that only show content.</li><li value=\\"8\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Verify: Remove debug screens from production</strong><br>Wrap every debug menu, feature flag screen and test endpoint in if (__DEV__) or a build-time flag. Then install a release build and check they are gone.</li></ol><p style=\\"margin:0 0 8px\\"><strong>Moderate</strong></p><ol style=\\"margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px\\"><li value=\\"9\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Verify: Protect sensitive APIs from scripts</strong><br>Rate-limit login, signup and payment endpoints first. Then attest the app with Firebase App Check, or with App Attest and Play Integrity directly.</li><li value=\\"10\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Keep sensitive data out of Android backups</strong><br>Set android:allowBackup=&quot;false&quot; in AndroidManifest.xml, or exclude the sensitive files with dataExtractionRules (Android 12 and later) and fullBackupContent.</li><li value=\\"11\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Monitor your dependencies</strong><br>Turn on Dependabot or Renovate, and run this command in CI so a critical advisory fails the build.<br><code style=\\"font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:14px\\">npm audit --audit-level=critical</code></li><li value=\\"12\\" style=\\"margin:0 0 12px\\"><strong>Verify: Run a security scanner in CI</strong><br>Add rnsec to your pull request pipeline, with the command at the end of this email, so it blocks changes that introduce a vulnerability.</li></ol><p style=\\"margin:0 0 16px\\"></p><p style=\\"margin:0 0 16px\\">Run rnsec on every pull request so these stay fixed:<br><code style=\\"font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:14px\\">npx rnsec scan --changed-files main --silent</code></p><p style=\\"margin:0 0 16px\\">Want us to audit the codebase itself? <a href=\\"https://weshipit.today/audit\\" style=\\"color:#2563eb\\">https://weshipit.today/audit</a></p><p style=\\"margin:0 0 16px\\">Stuck on one fix? Reply with its number.</p><p style=\\"margin:32px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:#64748b\\"><a href=\\"https://weshipit.today/api/lm/unsubscribe?t=abc\\" style=\\"color:#2563eb\\">Unsubscribe</a></p></div></body></html>",
  "subject": "Your security report: 25/100, 12 fixes in order",
  "text": "25/100. High exposure.
0 of 12 checks already pass. Here are the other 12, in the order to tackle them.

CRITICAL
1. Move secret keys out of the app
   Anything in your JS bundle, app.config or EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables can be read from the app binary. Move each secret behind your own API, then rotate it: the old key is already exposed.
   $ npx rnsec scan
2. Verify: Block plain HTTP traffic
   Remove usesCleartextTraffic from AndroidManifest.xml and NSAllowsArbitraryLoads from Info.plist. If a dev server needs plain HTTP, allow only that domain, in a debug-only config.
   $ git grep -nE \\"usesCleartextTraffic|NSAllowsArbitraryLoads\\"
3. Enforce authorization on the backend
   Anyone can call your API without the app. Turn on Row Level Security on every Supabase table, or write Firebase Security Rules, then make each endpoint check who is asking and what they own.

HIGH
4. Verify: Store auth tokens in secure storage
   AsyncStorage and MMKV write plain files that a backup or a rooted device can read. Store access and refresh tokens with expo-secure-store (or react-native-keychain). This command lists the places that write a token today.
   $ git grep -nE \\"(AsyncStorage|MMKV|storage)\\\\.set.*[Tt]oken\\"
5. Clean secrets out of production logs
   Strip console.log from production builds with babel-plugin-transform-remove-console, and drop tokens, passwords and personal data in Sentry’s beforeSend.
6. Validate deep link parameters
   Treat every deep link as untrusted input. Validate each parameter against what the screen expects, and ask for confirmation before a payment, a deletion or an account change.
7. Verify: Lock down your WebViews
   Set originWhitelist to your own domains, and check event.nativeEvent.url in onMessage before acting on a message. Turn off javaScriptEnabled on WebViews that only show content.
8. Verify: Remove debug screens from production
   Wrap every debug menu, feature flag screen and test endpoint in if (__DEV__) or a build-time flag. Then install a release build and check they are gone.

MODERATE
9. Verify: Protect sensitive APIs from scripts
   Rate-limit login, signup and payment endpoints first. Then attest the app with Firebase App Check, or with App Attest and Play Integrity directly.
10. Keep sensitive data out of Android backups
   Set android:allowBackup=\\"false\\" in AndroidManifest.xml, or exclude the sensitive files with dataExtractionRules (Android 12 and later) and fullBackupContent.
11. Monitor your dependencies
   Turn on Dependabot or Renovate, and run this command in CI so a critical advisory fails the build.
   $ npm audit --audit-level=critical
12. Verify: Run a security scanner in CI
   Add rnsec to your pull request pipeline, with the command at the end of this email, so it blocks changes that introduce a vulnerability.

Run rnsec on every pull request so these stay fixed:
$ npx rnsec scan --changed-files main --silent

Want us to audit the codebase itself? https://weshipit.today/audit

Stuck on one fix? Reply with its number.

Unsubscribe: https://weshipit.today/api/lm/unsubscribe?t=abc",
}
`;

